; FILED: an exact bignum-with-ratnum result is unrepresentable in the VM.
;
; The VM's rational is int64 numerator over int64 denominator (VmRational), so
; a bignum combined with a ratnum has no exact representation: it takes the
; same correctly-rounded inexact fallback the int64-overflow case uses.  Native
; carries exact bignum rationals and prints them.
;
; This is a REPRESENTATION gap, not a dispatch defect.  The dispatch defect
; that used to hide it — the bignum being read as the integer 0, so that
; (+ <bignum> 1/3) answered 1/3 and (/ 1/3 <bignum>) was a spurious
; DIVIDE BY ZERO — is fixed and gated by
; tests/vm_parity/corpus/52_numeric_tag_dispatch.esk.
;
; Closing this needs bignum components in VmRational (a numeric-tower feature),
; tracked with found/bignum_exact_rational.esk.
;
; native -r : 110680464442257309697/3   36893488147419103232/3   1/110680464442257309696
; vm        : 36893488147419103000      12297829382473034000     9.03501810404587e-21

(define big (* 4611686018427387904 8))
(define rat (/ 1 3))
(display (+ big rat)) (newline)
(display (* big rat)) (newline)
(display (/ rat big)) (newline)
